{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-03-17T16:04:33.430Z","tool_id":"run_shell_command_1773763472903_0","status":"success","output":"# مرجع قاعدة البيانات المعجمية — Arabic Dictionary DB Reference\n\n> اقرأ هذا الملف أولاً — قبل أي استعلام.\n> Read this file first — before any query.\n\n---\n\n## أ. نظرة عامة — Overview\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Database engine | SQLite 3 (WAL journal, FTS5) |\n| Total entries | 760,660 |\n| Dictionaries | 107 |\n| Definitions | 614,227 |\n| Examples | 86,031 (quran/hadith/poetry/usage/proverb) |\n| Size on disk | ~2.1 GB |\n\n### مصادر البيانات — Data Sources\n\n| source_type | Dictionaries | Entries | Content |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ocr` | 5 | 109,769 | Gemini-extracted from classical Arabic lexicons (Al-Waseet, Al-Kabir). Best roots (`root_source='ocr'`). Full multi-sense definitions. |\n| `hawramani` | 51 | 233,465 | Classical+medieval lexicons via arabiclexicon.hawramani.com. Rich definitions. Root often NULL (headword IS the root). |\n| `arabterm` | 51 | 417,426 | Modern multilingual terminology (ALECSO). Has `translation_en`, `translation_fr`, `domain`. No definitions_text. |\n\n---\n\n## ب. كيفية الاستعلام — How to Query\n\n### الأمر الأساسي — Base command\n\n```bash\nsqlite3 -json \"DB_PATH\" \"SELECT ...\"\n```\n\n`-json` returns a JSON array. Arabic text prints correctly.\n\n> **Important:** Replace `DB_PATH` with the actual database path provided in the user prompt.\n\n### تحسين الأداء — Performance (run once)\n\n```bash\nsqlite3 \"DB_PATH\" \"PRAGMA cache_size=-64000; PRAGMA mmap_size=3000000000; SELECT 'OK';\"\n```\n\n### تسوية النص العربي — Arabic Normalization\n\nThe `headword_norm` column is already normalized: diacritics stripped, alef forms (أإآ) → ا, ya (ى) → ي, tatweel (ـ) removed.\n\n**When you construct a search term**, apply the same normalization:\n- Strip diacritics: remove all harakat (◌َ◌ُ◌ِ◌ّ◌ْ◌ً◌ٌ◌ٍ etc.)\n- Normalize: أإآ → ا, ى → ي, remove ـ\n\nExample: lemma `كَتَبَ` → search for `headword_norm = 'كتب'`\n\n### وعي الـ«ال» — ال-Awareness\n\n**~20% of entries** (154K) store nouns with the definite article ال in `headword_norm`.\n**Always search BOTH forms:**\n\n```sql\nWHERE headword_norm IN ('ملاذ', 'الملاذ')\n```\n\nIf the lemma already starts with ال, search both the full form and the stripped form:\n```sql\n-- lemma = 'الكتاب'\nWHERE headword_norm IN ('الكتاب', 'كتاب')\n```\n\n---\n\n## ج. الجداول — Schema\n\n### entries (760,660 rows)\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE entries (\n    id              INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    dictionary_id   INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES dictionaries(id),\n    headword        TEXT NOT NULL,           -- with diacritics: كَتَبَ\n    headword_bare   TEXT NOT NULL,           -- diacritics stripped: كتب\n    headword_norm   TEXT NOT NULL,           -- fully normalized (search on this)\n    root            TEXT,                    -- trilateral root: كتب (space-free)\n    root_source     TEXT,                    -- 'ocr' | 'lane' | 'camel' | NULL\n    pos             TEXT,                    -- verb/noun/adj/particle/proper_noun/phrase\n    form            TEXT,                    -- verb form I–X, NULL for non-verbs\n    is_partial      INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    definitions_text TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '', -- flattened definitions (OCR/Hawramani)\n    translation_en  TEXT,                    -- ARABTERM only\n    translation_fr  TEXT,                    -- ARABTERM only\n    domain          TEXT,                    -- ARABTERM only\n    external_id     TEXT                     -- dedup key\n);\n```\n\n**Root source priority:** ocr (most accurate) > lane > camel > NULL.\n\n### dictionaries (107 rows)\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE dictionaries (\n    id            INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    key           TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,       -- e.g. 'Al_Waseet'\n    name_ar       TEXT,                       -- المعجم الوسيط\n    name_en       TEXT,                       -- Al-Mu'jam Al-Wasit\n    source_type   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ocr', -- 'ocr' | 'hawramani' | 'arabterm'\n    group_key     TEXT,\n    period        TEXT,                        -- 'modern' | 'classical'\n    author        TEXT,\n    death_year    INTEGER,                     -- CE year of author's death\n    metadata      TEXT DEFAULT '{}'\n);\n```\n\n### definitions (614,227 rows) — per-sense breakdown\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE definitions (\n    id          INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    entry_id    INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES entries(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    sense_index INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,  -- 0-based\n    text        TEXT NOT NULL,\n    is_raw      INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0   -- 1 = unparsed blob (Hawramani)\n);\n```\n\n### examples (86,031 rows) — citations\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE examples (\n    id          INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    entry_id    INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES entries(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    idx         INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    type        TEXT,     -- 'quran' | 'hadith' | 'poetry' | 'usage' | 'proverb'\n    text        TEXT NOT NULL,\n    attribution TEXT\n);\n```\n\n### plurals (24,466), derived_forms (50,191), cross_refs (10,453)\n\nAll follow the same pattern: `entry_id FK`, `idx`, `text`.\n\n### provenance (552,601 rows) — source tracking\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE provenance (\n    entry_id          INTEGER PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES entries(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    page_number       TEXT,\n    page_file         TEXT,          -- e.g. 'page_0031'\n    entry_index       INTEGER,\n    volume            TEXT,\n    hawramani_post_id INTEGER,\n    hawramani_slug    TEXT,\n    source_uri        TEXT           -- e.g. 'https://arabiclexicon.hawramani.com/'\n);\n```\n\n### FTS5 Virtual Tables\n\n```sql\n-- Arabic full-text search\nCREATE VIRTUAL TABLE entries_fts USING fts5(\n    headword, headword_bare, headword_norm, root, definitions_text,\n    content=entries, content_rowid=id,\n    tokenize='unicode61 remove_diacritics 2'\n);\n\n-- Multilingual search (ARABTERM translations)\nCREATE VIRTUAL TABLE entries_translations_fts USING fts5(\n    translation_en, translation_fr, domain,\n    content=entries, content_rowid=id,\n    tokenize='unicode61 remove_diacritics 2'\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n## د. كفاءة الاستعلام — Query Efficiency (CRITICAL)\n\n**Each query costs a tool-call turn. Minimize total queries by batching aggressively.**\n\n### القواعد الذهبية — Golden Rules\n\n1. **Batch ALL lemmas in one headword query.** Never query lemmas one-by-one.\n   Include both forms (bare + ال) for every lemma in a single `WHERE headword_norm IN (...)`:\n   ```sql\n   -- 3 lemmas = 1 query (not 3)\n   WHERE headword_norm IN ('ترامواي','الترامواي','تلفريك','التلفريك','قطار هوائي','القطار الهوائي')\n   ```\n\n2. **English bridge = ONE query with ALL English lemmas.** Combine all OEWN lemmas:\n   ```sql\n   WHERE entries_translations_fts MATCH 'translation_en:\"tramway\" OR translation_en:\"tram\" OR translation_en:\"cable car\" OR translation_en:\"ropeway\" OR translation_en:\"aerial tramway\"'\n   ```\n   Never run a second English bridge query. If you need more English terms, you should have included them in the first query.\n\n3. **Arabic FTS = at most 2 queries.** One broad keyword search from the definition, one for compound candidate terms. Never run 4-5 overlapping FTS queries.\n\n4. **Never re-query the same lemma.** Note the `entry_id` values from your first headword query. Use `WHERE entry_id IN (id1, id2, ...)` for enrichment — never re-query by headword_norm for data you already retrieved.\n\n5. **Batch Step 0.5 candidate validation** into one or two headword queries:\n   ```sql\n   -- Validate ALL generated candidates at once\n   WHERE headword_norm IN ('candidate1','الcandidate1','candidate2','الcandidate2',...)\n   ```\n\n6. **Enrich by entry_id, not by headword.** For examples, definitions, plurals — always use entry_id from earlier results:\n   ```sql\n   SELECT ... FROM examples WHERE entry_id IN (857316, 68214, 362484) ...\n   ```\n\n### Target query budget per synset\n\n| Phase | Queries | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Step 0: Evidence | 1 | Batch headword lookup for ALL lemmas |\n| Step 0: Evidence | 1 | Examples + enrichment by entry_id |\n| Step 0: Evidence | 0-1 | Root inference (only if needed, already in headword results) |\n| Step 0.5: Generation | 1 | English bridge (ALL English lemmas at once) |\n| Step 0.5: Generation | 1 | Arabic FTS keyword search (broad) |\n| Step 0.5: Validation | 1 | Batch headword lookup for ALL candidates |\n| Step 1: Validation | 0-1 | Follow-up if specific evidence needed |\n| Step 5: Enrichment | 0-1 | Examples/plurals by entry_id |\n| **Total** | **~6-8** | **(not 20+)** |\n\n---\n\n## ه. الاستعلامات المُثبتة — Proven Query Patterns\n\n### مجموعة الأعمدة المشتركة — Shared Column Set\n\nFor brevity, templates below use `{ENTRY_COLS}` to mean:\n\n```sql\n    e.id AS entry_id, e.dictionary_id,\n    e.headword, e.headword_bare, e.headword_norm,\n    e.root, e.root_source, e.pos, e.form,\n    e.definitions_text, e.translation_en, e.translation_fr, e.domain,\n    d.key AS dict_key, d.name_ar AS dict_name_ar, d.name_en AS dict_name_en,\n    d.source_type AS dict_source_type, d.period AS dict_period,\n    d.author AS dict_author, d.death_year AS dict_death_year\n```\n\n> **Tip:** Select fewer columns when you only need specific fields (e.g., `e.headword, e.definitions_text, d.name_ar`). This reduces output size.\n\n---\n\n### ١. المطابقة الدقيقة — Batch Headword Lookup (ALL lemmas at once)\n\n**الغرض:** Find all dictionary entries matching ANY synset lemma. **This is your first and most important query — include ALL lemmas.**\n\n```sql\nSELECT {ENTRY_COLS}\nFROM entries e\nJOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id = d.id\nWHERE e.headword_norm IN (\n    '<lemma1_norm>', 'ال<lemma1_norm>',\n    '<lemma2_norm>', 'ال<lemma2_norm>',\n    '<lemma3_norm>', 'ال<lemma3_norm>'\n)\nORDER BY e.headword_norm, d.source_type, d.death_year ASC NULLS LAST, d.name_en;\n```\n\n**Example (3 lemmas = 1 query):**\n```bash\nsqlite3 -json \"DB_PATH\" \"SELECT e.id AS entry_id, e.headword, e.headword_norm, e.root, e.root_source, e.definitions_text, e.translation_en, e.domain, d.name_ar, d.source_type, d.period FROM entries e JOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id=d.id WHERE e.headword_norm IN ('ترامواي','الترامواي','تلفريك','التلفريك','قطار هوائي','القطار الهوائي') ORDER BY e.headword_norm, d.source_type, d.death_year ASC NULLS LAST;\"\n```\n\n**For multiword lemmas** that return empty: also query component words, but batch them together in ONE follow-up query:\n```sql\nWHERE e.headword_norm IN ('قطار','القطار','هوائي','الهوائي')\n```\n\n**Note entry_ids** from this query — you will reuse them for enrichment. Never re-query the same lemma by headword_norm.\n\n---\n\n### ٢. استنتاج الجذر — Root Inference (from headword results)\n\n**الغرض:** Find the trilateral root for a lemma, prioritizing more reliable sources.\n\n**First:** Check the `root` and `root_source` columns already returned in Query ١. Often sufficient.\n\n**Only if root is NULL in all results:**\n```sql\nSELECT DISTINCT e.root, e.root_source\nFROM entries e\nWHERE e.headword_norm IN ('<norm>', 'ال<norm>')\n  AND e.root IS NOT NULL\nORDER BY CASE e.root_source\n    WHEN 'ocr'  THEN 1\n    WHEN 'lane' THEN 2\n    WHEN 'camel' THEN 3\n    ELSE 4\nEND;\n```\n\n**Root source priority:** ocr (most accurate) > lane > camel > NULL. The first row has the most reliable root.\n\n---\n\n### ٣. عائلة الجذر — Root Family (per-root)\n\n**الغرض:** Find sibling derivations sharing the same root — useful for lemma generation and validation.\n\n```sql\nSELECT {ENTRY_COLS}\nFROM entries e\nJOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id = d.id\nWHERE (e.root = '<root>' OR e.headword_norm = '<root>')\n  AND e.id NOT IN (<already_seen_ids>)\nORDER BY d.source_type, d.death_year ASC NULLS LAST, d.name_en\nLIMIT 200;\n```\n\n**Important:** The `OR e.headword_norm = '<root>'` clause catches Hawramani entries where the headword IS the root form but the `root` column is NULL. Use `-1` if you have no IDs to exclude: `AND e.id NOT IN (-1)`.\n\n---\n\n### ٤. الشواهد والإثراء بالمعرّف — Examples & Enrichment (by entry_id)\n\n**الغرض:** Retrieve examples, definitions, plurals for entries you already found.\n\n**Always use entry_id from earlier queries — never re-query by headword_norm.**\n\n```sql\nSELECT ex.entry_id, e.headword, d.name_ar,\n       ex.type, ex.text AS example_text, ex.attribution\nFROM examples ex\nJOIN entries e ON ex.entry_id = e.id\nJOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id = d.id\nWHERE ex.entry_id IN (<entry_ids_from_query_1>)\nORDER BY CASE ex.type\n    WHEN 'quran'  THEN 1\n    WHEN 'hadith' THEN 2\n    WHEN 'poetry' THEN 3\n    WHEN 'prose'  THEN 4\n    WHEN 'usage'  THEN 5\n    ELSE 6\nEND, ex.idx;\n```\n\n---\n\n### ٥. البحث العكسي — Reverse Lookup / FTS (per-lemma)\n\n**الغرض:** Find entries that MENTION this lemma in their headword or definitions (synonym chains, cross-references).\n\n```sql\nSELECT {ENTRY_COLS}\nFROM entries e\nJOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id = d.id\nWHERE e.id IN (\n    SELECT rowid FROM entries_fts\n    WHERE entries_fts MATCH '{headword headword_bare definitions_text}:\"<bare_lemma>\"'\n    ORDER BY bm25(entries_fts, 10.0, 5.0, 5.0, 3.0, 1.0)\n    LIMIT 100\n)\nAND e.headword_norm NOT IN ('<norm>', 'ال<norm>')\nORDER BY d.source_type, d.death_year ASC NULLS LAST, d.name_en;\n```\n\n**FTS5 notes:**\n- Quote the search term with double quotes inside the MATCH: `\"ملاذ\"`\n- Column filter `{headword headword_bare definitions_text}:` restricts search to those 3 columns\n- BM25 weights: headword(10), headword_bare(5), headword_norm(5), root(3), definitions_text(1)\n\n---\n\n### ٦. البحث بالكلمات المفتاحية — FTS Keyword Search (per-synset, ONE query)\n\n**الغرض:** Search by Arabic keywords from the synset's definition to find related entries.\n\n**Combine all keywords into ONE query. Include both single words and compound terms:**\n\n```sql\nSELECT {ENTRY_COLS}\nFROM entries e\nJOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id = d.id\nWHERE e.id IN (\n    SELECT rowid FROM entries_fts\n    WHERE entries_fts MATCH '\"<keyword1>\" OR \"<keyword2>\" OR \"<compound term>\" OR \"<keyword3>\"'\n    ORDER BY bm25(entries_fts, 10.0, 5.0, 5.0, 3.0, 1.0)\n    LIMIT 50\n)\nAND e.id NOT IN (<already_seen_ids>)\nORDER BY d.source_type, d.name_en;\n```\n\n**Tip:** Extract meaningful content words from the Arabic definition (skip stop words like من، في، على، إلى، عن، هو، هي، هذا، ما، لا، أن، كل). Normalize them (strip diacritics, أإآ→ا, ى→ي).\n\n---\n\n### ٧. الجسر الإنجليزي — English Bridge (per-synset, ONE query)\n\n**الغرض:** Use English lemmas from OEWN to find ARABTERM entries with Arabic translations.\n\n**Include ALL English lemmas and their synonyms in ONE query:**\n\n```sql\nSELECT {ENTRY_COLS}\nFROM entries e\nJOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id = d.id\nWHERE e.id IN (\n    SELECT rowid FROM entries_translations_fts\n    WHERE entries_translations_fts MATCH 'translation_en:\"<en_lemma1>\" OR translation_en:\"<en_lemma2>\" OR translation_en:\"<en_lemma3>\" OR translation_en:\"<en_lemma4>\"'\n    ORDER BY bm25(entries_translations_fts, 5.0, 3.0, 1.0)\n    LIMIT 50\n)\nAND e.id NOT IN (<already_seen_ids>)\nORDER BY d.source_type, d.name_en;\n```\n\n**Include related English terms too** (not just OEWN lemmas). E.g., for \"cable car\" synset, also add \"gondola\", \"ropeway\", \"aerial\", \"telpher\" in the same query.\n\n---\n\n### ٨. التصفية حسب الصنف — POS-filtered Root Family (per-synset)\n\n**الغرض:** Restrict root family to entries matching the synset's POS.\n\n```sql\nSELECT {ENTRY_COLS}\nFROM entries e\nJOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id = d.id\nWHERE e.root = '<root>'\n  AND e.pos = '<pos>'\nORDER BY d.source_type, d.name_en;\n```\n\nPOS values: `noun`, `verb`, `adj`, `particle`, `proper_noun`, `phrase`.\n\n---\n\n### ٩. التصفية حسب المجال — Domain-filtered ARABTERM (per-synset)\n\n**الغرض:** Find same-domain technical terms in ARABTERM.\n\n```sql\nSELECT {ENTRY_COLS}\nFROM entries e\nJOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id = d.id\nWHERE e.domain = '<domain>'\n  AND e.headword_norm != '<lemma_norm>'\n  AND d.source_type = 'arabterm'\nORDER BY d.name_en\nLIMIT 30;\n```\n\n---\n\n## و. استعلامات الإثراء — Enrichment Queries\n\n**After finding entries, use their `entry_id` values for enrichment. Batch all IDs in ONE query per child table.**\n\n### التعريفات المُفصّلة — Definitions (per-sense)\n\n```sql\nSELECT entry_id, sense_index, text, is_raw\nFROM definitions\nWHERE entry_id IN (<ids>)\nORDER BY entry_id, sense_index;\n```\n\n### الشواهد — Examples\n\n```sql\nSELECT entry_id, idx, type, text, attribution\nFROM examples\nWHERE entry_id IN (<ids>)\nORDER BY entry_id, idx;\n```\n\n### الجموع — Plurals\n\n```sql\nSELECT entry_id, idx, text FROM plurals WHERE entry_id IN (<ids>) ORDER BY entry_id, idx;\n```\n\n### المشتقات — Derived Forms\n\n```sql\nSELECT entry_id, idx, text FROM derived_forms WHERE entry_id IN (<ids>) ORDER BY entry_id, idx;\n```\n\n### الإحالات — Cross References\n\n```sql\nSELECT entry_id, idx, text FROM cross_refs WHERE entry_id IN (<ids>) ORDER BY entry_id, idx;\n```\n\n### المصدر — Provenance\n\n```sql\nSELECT entry_id, page_number, page_file, volume, source_uri\nFROM provenance WHERE entry_id IN (<ids>);\n```\n\n### استعلام إثراء مُدمج — Combined enrichment (recommended)\n\n**Fetch examples + definitions + plurals in ONE compound query** to save turns:\n\n```bash\nsqlite3 -json \"DB_PATH\" \"\nSELECT 'def' AS _table, entry_id, sense_index AS idx, text, NULL AS type, NULL AS attribution FROM definitions WHERE entry_id IN (<ids>)\nUNION ALL\nSELECT 'ex' AS _table, entry_id, idx, text, type, attribution FROM examples WHERE entry_id IN (<ids>)\nUNION ALL\nSELECT 'pl' AS _table, entry_id, idx, text, NULL, NULL FROM plurals WHERE entry_id IN (<ids>)\nORDER BY entry_id, _table, idx;\n\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## ز. إحصائيات سريعة — Quick Stats\n\n```sql\nSELECT\n    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM entries) AS total_entries,\n    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM dictionaries) AS total_dictionaries,\n    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM definitions) AS total_definitions,\n    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM examples) AS total_examples;\n```\n\n---\n\n## ح. الأدلة المُسبقة الجلب — Pre-fetched Evidence\n\nIf `evidence.json` exists in the synset's prepared directory, it contains pre-computed\nresults for the three deterministic queries: headword lookup (Pattern ١), combined\nenrichment (section و), and English bridge (Pattern ٧).\n\n**Read `evidence.json` first — it replaces your first 3 queries.**\n\n### الهيكل — Structure\n\n```json\n{\n  \"headword_entries\": [...],    // Pattern ١ results (all lemmas + ال-forms)\n  \"enrichment\": [...],          // Combined definitions + examples + plurals by entry_id\n  \"english_bridge\": [...],      // Pattern ٧ results (all OEWN English lemmas)\n  \"query_meta\": {\n    \"lemma_terms\": [\"كيان\", \"الكيان\", ...],\n    \"english_terms\": [\"entity\", \"being\", ...],\n    \"entry_ids\": [766454, 534694, ...],\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-12T10:00:00Z\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### الاستعلامات المتبقية — Remaining Queries\n\nWhen `evidence.json` is available, you still need to run yourself:\n\n| # | Query | Purpose |\n|---|-------|---------|\n| 1 | Pattern ٦ (Arabic FTS keyword) | You choose the keywords from the definition |\n| 2 | Pattern ١ (candidate validation) | Validate Step 0.5 candidates by headword |\n\n**Target: ~2-3 queries per synset** when evidence.json is available (down from 6-8).\n\n### الرجوع — Fallback\n\nIf `evidence.json` does NOT exist, run the standard query sequence as documented above:\nPattern ١ → enrichment → Pattern ٧ → Pattern ٦ → candidate validation.\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# مخطط مخرجات المراجعة — Review Pipeline v2.0 Output Template\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n#\n# هذا الملف يحدد البنية الكاملة لمخرجات YAML لكل مجموعة ترادفية.\n# This file defines the complete YAML output structure for each synset review.\n#\n# ── اصطلاحات — Conventions ──\n# - Field names: English (snake_case)\n# - Analysis text: Arabic\n# - Decision enums: English lowercase\n# - DRY: omit fields with null/empty/false values\n# - {auto} placeholder IDs: resolved downstream by apply_reviews_v2.py\n# - {synset_id}: replaced by the actual synset ID being reviewed\n# - Command names: exact WordnetEditor method names (English)\n#\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n# ── المرحلة ١: المراجعة والتوليد (بدون أدلة) ──────────────\n# Stage 1: Review + Generate (no evidence)\n#\n# The reviewer first reads the MASKED synset info (no lemmas visible),\n# then generates 4 fully-diacritized candidate lemmas. Then reads the\n# full synset info and produces an initial linguistic assessment.\nstage1_review:\n  assessment:\n    concerns:                           # list of issues found\n      - \"...\"\n    observations: \"...\"                 # free-form Arabic analysis\n  blind_candidates:                     # 4 candidates, NO evidence yet\n    - lemma: \"لَمَّة\"                   # full tashkeel mandatory\n      generation_method: ishtiqaq       # majaz | ishtiqaq | tarkib | taarib\n      justification: \"...\"\n    - lemma: \"مُرَشَّح٢\"\n      generation_method: tarkib\n      justification: \"...\"\n    - lemma: \"مُرَشَّح٣\"\n      generation_method: majaz\n      justification: \"...\"\n    - lemma: \"مُرَشَّح٤\"\n      generation_method: ishtiqaq\n      justification: \"...\"\n\n\n# ── المرحلة ٢: جمع الأدلة ────────────────────────────────\n# Stage 2: Evidence Gathering (interactive, in-session)\n#\n# The reviewer queries the Arabic dictionary DB via sqlite3 -json\n# to gather evidence for ALL lemmas (existing + Stage 1 candidates).\n# Target query budget: 5-8 queries total.\nstage2_evidence:\n  per_lemma:                            # covers BOTH existing lemmas AND Stage 1 candidates\n    - lemma: \"لَمَّة\"\n      confirm:                          # dictionary text supporting this lemma for the synset\n        - text: \"«نص المعجم»\"\n          source: \"اسم المعجم\"\n      contradicts:                      # dictionary text contradicting this usage\n        - text: \"«نص المعجم»\"\n          source: \"اسم المعجم\"\n          conflict: \"سبب التعارض\"\n      expands:                          # dictionary text expanding on this meaning\n        - text: \"«نص المعجم»\"\n          source: \"اسم المعجم\"\n          addition: \"ما يضيفه الدليل\"\n      # When ALL three categories are empty, use this instead:\n      # evidence_status: \"no_material_found\"\n\n\n# ── المرحلة ٣: التحليل اللغوي للّمات ────────────────────\n# Stage 3: Lemma Linguistic Analysis\n#\n# For each lemma (existing + candidates), produce a linguistic analysis\n# with include/exclude decision and generate actions.\nstage3_analysis:\n  per_lemma:\n    # ── existing lemma example ──\n    - lemma: \"لَمَّة\"                   # exactly as in synset_info\n      decision: confirmed               # confirmed | removed\n      decision_reason: \"...\"            # Arabic explanation\n      evidence_assessment:\n        case: confirm_only              # confirm_only | mixed | contradicts_only | no_material\n      mwe_check:\n        is_mwe: false\n        # mwe_type: idafi              # idafi | wasfi | mazji (only if is_mwe: true)\n      # nuance_differentiation: \"...\"  # mandatory if confirmed — how this lemma differs from siblings\n      actions:\n        - command: update_lemma\n          params:\n            entry_id: \"{auto}\"\n            new_lemma: \"لَمَّة\"\n\n    # ── Stage 1 candidate example ──\n    - lemma: \"مُرَشَّح\"\n      source: stage1                    # mark Stage 1 candidates\n      decision: confirmed               # confirmed | removed\n      decision_reason: \"...\"\n      evidence_assessment:\n        case: confirm_only\n      mwe_check:\n        is_mwe: false\n      actions:\n        - command: create_entry\n          params: {lemma: \"مُرَشَّح\", pos: n}\n        - command: add_sense\n          params: {entry_id: \"{auto}\", synset_id: \"{synset_id}\"}\n\n    # ── removed lemma example (minimal) ──\n    - lemma: \"لَمَّة_مَرْفوضة\"\n      decision: removed\n      decision_reason: \"...\"\n      # No actions needed for removed lemmas\n\n  # Synset-level corrections (if needed)\n  # synset_actions:\n  #   - command: update_synset\n  #     params: {synset_id: \"{synset_id}\", pos: n}\n\n\n# ── المرحلة ٤: التعريف والأمثلة ──────────────────────────\n# Stage 4: Definitions & Examples\n#\n# Assess and enrich the synset's Arabic definition and examples.\n# Only covers CONFIRMED lemmas from Stage 3.\nstage4_content:\n  definition:\n    current: \"التعريف الحالي\"            # current Arabic definition (from synset_info)\n    assessment:\n      decision: revise                  # retain | revise\n      reason: \"...\"                     # why revise/retain\n    authored:                           # new/revised definitions (only if revise)\n      - type: terminological            # terminological | linguistic | encyclopedic\n        text: \"...\"\n        quality_check:\n          genus_present: true\n          differentia_present: true\n          circular: false\n      - type: linguistic\n        text: \"...\"\n        quality_check:\n          genus_present: true\n          differentia_present: true\n          circular: false\n      - type: encyclopedic\n        text: \"...\"\n        # quality_check omitted if not applicable\n    actions:\n      - command: update_definition\n        params: {synset_id: \"{synset_id}\", definition_index: 0, text: \"...\"}\n      - command: add_definition\n        params: {synset_id: \"{synset_id}\", text: \"...\"}\n\n  examples:\n    per_lemma:                          # one example per confirmed lemma\n      - lemma: \"لَمَّة\"\n        examples:\n          - text: \"...\"\n            type: usage                 # usage | quran | hadith | poetry | proverb\n            source: \"مؤلَّف\"            # optional — if from a known source\n    actions:\n      - command: add_synset_example\n        params: {synset_id: \"{synset_id}\", text: \"...\"}\n      - command: add_sense_example\n        params: {sense_id: \"{auto}\", text: \"...\"}\n\n\n# ── المرحلة ٥: الإثراء (البيانات الوصفية) ─────────────────\n# Stage 5: Enrichment (metadata)\n#\n# Populate entries, senses, and synset with structured metadata,\n# packed into the WN-LMF `note` key for XML round-trip safety.\nstage5_enrichment:\n  per_entry:\n    # Single-word entry\n    - lemma: \"كِيَان\"\n      entry_id: \"{auto}\"\n      root: \"كون\"\n      maqayis_quote: \"«الْكَافُ وَالْوَاوُ وَالنُّونُ أَصْلٌ صَحِيحٌ...»\"\n    # MWE entry — per-word roots\n    - lemma: \"ذَكَاء اصْطِنَاعِيّ\"\n      entry_id: \"{auto}\"\n      roots:\n        - word: \"ذكاء\"\n          root: \"ذكو\"\n          maqayis_quote: \"«الذَّالُ وَالْكَافُ...»\"\n        - word: \"اصطناعي\"\n          root: \"صنع\"\n          maqayis_quote: \"«الصَّادُ وَالنُّونُ...»\"\n\n  per_sense:\n    - lemma: \"كِيَان\"\n      sense_id: \"{auto}\"\n      nuance: \"...\"                     # MANDATORY — how this lemma differs from siblings\n      mwe: false                        # true only for MWEs\n\n  synset:\n    cultural_fit: native                # native | lexical_gap | phraset | omission\n\n  actions:\n    # Entry-level note (single-word)\n    - command: set_metadata\n      params:\n        entity_type: entry\n        entity_id: \"{auto}\"\n        key: note\n        value: '{\"root\":\"كون\",\"maqayis\":\"«...»\"}'\n    # Entry-level note (MWE)\n    - command: set_metadata\n      params:\n        entity_type: entry\n        entity_id: \"{auto}\"\n        key: note\n        value: '{\"roots\":[{\"word\":\"ذكاء\",\"root\":\"ذكو\",\"maqayis\":\"«...»\"},{\"word\":\"اصطناعي\",\"root\":\"صنع\",\"maqayis\":\"«...»\"}]}'\n    # Sense-level note\n    - command: set_metadata\n      params:\n        entity_type: sense\n        entity_id: \"{auto}\"\n        key: note\n        value: '{\"nuance\":\"...\",\"mwe\":false}'\n    # Synset-level note\n    - command: set_metadata\n      params:\n        entity_type: synset\n        entity_id: \"{synset_id}\"\n        key: note\n        value: '{\"cultural_fit\":\"native\"}'\n    # Confidence\n    - command: set_confidence\n      params:\n        entity_type: synset\n        entity_id: \"{synset_id}\"\n        score: 0.85\n\n\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# مرجع الحقول — Field Reference\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n# ── Stage 1 Fields ──────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# stage1_review.assessment.concerns:\n#   type: list[str]\n#   description: List of issues found during initial assessment\n#\n# stage1_review.assessment.observations:\n#   type: str\n#   description: Free-form Arabic linguistic analysis\n#\n# stage1_review.blind_candidates[].lemma:\n#   type: str\n#   description: Fully diacritized Arabic lemma\n#   required: true\n#\n# stage1_review.blind_candidates[].generation_method:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [majaz, ishtiqaq, tarkib, taarib]\n#   description: |\n#     majaz     = semantic extension (metaphor/metonymy from existing Arabic word)\n#     ishtiqaq  = derivation from Arabic root on standard pattern\n#     tarkib    = compounding (idafi, wasfi, or mazji)\n#     taarib    = Arabization of foreign term (last resort)\n#\n# stage1_review.blind_candidates[].justification:\n#   type: str\n#   description: Arabic explanation of why this candidate fits the synset\n\n# ── Stage 2 Fields ──────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# stage2_evidence.per_lemma[].lemma:\n#   type: str\n#   required: true\n#\n# stage2_evidence.per_lemma[].confirm[]:\n#   type: list[{text: str, source: str}]\n#   description: Dictionary quotations supporting this lemma for the synset meaning\n#\n# stage2_evidence.per_lemma[].contradicts[]:\n#   type: list[{text: str, source: str, conflict: str}]\n#   description: Dictionary quotations contradicting this usage\n#\n# stage2_evidence.per_lemma[].expands[]:\n#   type: list[{text: str, source: str, addition: str}]\n#   description: Dictionary quotations expanding on this meaning\n#\n# stage2_evidence.per_lemma[].evidence_status:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [no_material_found]\n#   description: Only present when all three categories (confirm/contradicts/expands) are empty\n\n# ── Stage 3 Fields ──────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# stage3_analysis.per_lemma[].lemma:\n#   type: str\n#   required: true\n#\n# stage3_analysis.per_lemma[].source:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [stage1]\n#   description: Only present for Stage 1 candidates (absent for existing lemmas)\n#\n# stage3_analysis.per_lemma[].decision:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [confirmed, removed]\n#   required: true\n#\n# stage3_analysis.per_lemma[].decision_reason:\n#   type: str\n#   required: true\n#   description: Arabic explanation of the decision\n#\n# stage3_analysis.per_lemma[].evidence_assessment.case:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [confirm_only, mixed, contradicts_only, no_material]\n#\n# stage3_analysis.per_lemma[].mwe_check.is_mwe:\n#   type: bool\n#\n# stage3_analysis.per_lemma[].mwe_check.mwe_type:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [idafi, wasfi, mazji]\n#   description: Only present if is_mwe is true\n#\n# stage3_analysis.per_lemma[].actions[].command:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [remove_sense, update_lemma, update_entry, add_form, remove_form,\n#            create_entry, add_sense, update_synset,\n#            add_sense_relation, remove_sense_relation]\n#\n# ── Stage 3 Action Parameters ──\n#\n# remove_sense:\n#   sense_id: str        # \"{auto}\" or explicit sense ID\n#\n# update_lemma:\n#   entry_id: str        # \"{auto}\" or explicit entry ID\n#   new_lemma: str       # fully diacritized\n#\n# update_entry:\n#   entry_id: str\n#   pos: str             # n | v | a | r | s\n#\n# add_form:\n#   entry_id: str\n#   written_form: str\n#\n# remove_form:\n#   entry_id: str\n#   written_form: str\n#\n# create_entry:\n#   lemma: str           # fully diacritized\n#   pos: str             # n | v | a | r | s\n#\n# add_sense:\n#   entry_id: str        # \"{auto}\" — resolved from preceding create_entry\n#   synset_id: str       # \"{synset_id}\"\n#\n# update_synset:\n#   synset_id: str\n#   pos: str\n#\n# add_sense_relation:\n#   source_id: str       # sense ID\n#   relation_type: str   # e.g., \"derivation\", \"also\", \"similar\"\n#   target_id: str       # sense ID\n#\n# remove_sense_relation:\n#   source_id: str\n#   relation_type: str\n#   target_id: str\n\n# ── Stage 4 Fields ──────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# stage4_content.definition.current:\n#   type: str\n#   description: Current Arabic definition from synset_info\n#\n# stage4_content.definition.assessment.decision:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [retain, revise]\n#\n# stage4_content.definition.authored[].type:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [terminological, linguistic, encyclopedic]\n#\n# stage4_content.definition.authored[].text:\n#   type: str\n#   description: The authored definition text in Arabic\n#\n# stage4_content.definition.authored[].quality_check:\n#   type: object\n#   properties:\n#     genus_present: bool\n#     differentia_present: bool\n#     circular: bool\n#\n# stage4_content.examples.per_lemma[].examples[].type:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [usage, quran, hadith, poetry, proverb]\n#\n# ── Stage 4 Action Parameters ──\n#\n# update_definition:\n#   synset_id: str\n#   definition_index: int  # 0-based\n#   text: str\n#\n# add_definition:\n#   synset_id: str\n#   text: str\n#\n# remove_definition:\n#   synset_id: str\n#   definition_index: int  # 0-based\n#\n# add_synset_example:\n#   synset_id: str\n#   text: str\n#\n# remove_synset_example:\n#   synset_id: str\n#   example_index: int     # 0-based\n#\n# add_sense_example:\n#   sense_id: str          # \"{auto}\"\n#   text: str\n#\n# remove_sense_example:\n#   sense_id: str\n#   example_index: int     # 0-based\n\n# ── Stage 5 Fields ──────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# stage5_enrichment.per_entry[].root:\n#   type: str\n#   description: Trilateral (or bi/quadrilateral) root, space-free\n#\n# stage5_enrichment.per_entry[].maqayis_quote:\n#   type: str\n#   description: Verbatim quote from Maqayis al-Lugha (dictionary_id=151)\n#\n# stage5_enrichment.per_entry[].roots:\n#   type: list[{word: str, root: str, maqayis_quote: str}]\n#   description: Per-word roots for MWE entries (replaces root + maqayis_quote)\n#\n# stage5_enrichment.per_sense[].nuance:\n#   type: str\n#   required: true\n#   description: How this lemma differs semantically from siblings in the synset\n#\n# stage5_enrichment.per_sense[].mwe:\n#   type: bool\n#   description: true only for multi-word expressions\n#\n# stage5_enrichment.synset.cultural_fit:\n#   type: enum\n#   values: [native, lexical_gap, phraset, omission]\n#   description: |\n#     native       = concept has natural Arabic lexicalization\n#     lexical_gap  = concept exists in Arabic culture but lacks a dedicated term\n#     phraset      = concept only expressible as a phrase, not a single word\n#     omission     = concept is culturally foreign, needs careful introduction\n#\n# ── Stage 5 Action Parameters ──\n#\n# set_metadata:\n#   entity_type: str     # \"entry\" | \"sense\" | \"synset\"\n#   entity_id: str       # \"{auto}\" or \"{synset_id}\"\n#   key: str             # always \"note\" for enrichment\n#   value: str           # JSON string (note-packed)\n#\n# set_confidence:\n#   entity_type: str     # \"synset\" | \"sense\"\n#   entity_id: str\n#   score: float         # 0.0–1.0\n\n# ── Complete Action Type Catalog (19 types) ─────────────────\n#\n# Stage 3 (10 types):\n#   1.  remove_sense         — Lemma rejected\n#   2.  update_lemma         — Diacritics fix, spelling fix\n#   3.  update_entry         — Wrong POS on entry\n#   4.  add_form             — Add variant form\n#   5.  remove_form          — Remove incorrect form\n#   6.  create_entry         — New lemma approved\n#   7.  add_sense            — Link entry to synset\n#   8.  update_synset        — Wrong POS at synset level\n#   9.  add_sense_relation   — Derivation, sense antonymy\n#   10. remove_sense_relation — Wrong sense relation\n#\n# Stage 4 (7 types):\n#   11. update_definition     — Revise existing definition\n#   12. add_definition        — Add encyclopedic/linguistic def\n#   13. remove_definition     — Remove bad/duplicate def\n#   14. add_synset_example    — Add synset-level example\n#   15. remove_synset_example — Remove bad example\n#   16. add_sense_example     — Add sense-level example\n#   17. remove_sense_example  — Remove bad example\n#\n# Stage 5 (2 types):\n#   18. set_metadata          — Note-packed enrichment\n#   19. set_confidence        — Confidence scores\nid: awn4-13450179-n\nili: i107313\npos: n\ndefinition_ar: العملية العضوية للتقدم في العمر وظهور آثار زيادة السن\ndefinition_en: the organic process of growing older and showing the effects of increasing age\ndirect_hypernym:\n  id: awn4-13547313-n\n  definition_ar: عملية تحدث في الكائنات الحية"}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-03-17T16:04:48.201Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command_1773763488200_0","parameters":{"command":"sqlite3 -json /data/arabic_dict.db \"\nSELECT e.id AS entry_id, e.dictionary_id,\n       e.headword, e.headword_bare, e.headword_norm,\n       e.root, e.pos,\n       e.definitions_text, e.translation_en,\n       d.name_ar AS dict_name_ar, d.source_type\nFROM entries e\nJOIN dictionaries d ON e.dictionary_id = d.id\nWHERE e.headword_norm IN (\n    'تقدم في السن', 'التقدم في السن',\n    'شيخوخة', 'الشيخوخة',\n    'هرم', 'الهرم',\n    'اسنان', 'الاسنان',\n    'تشيخ', 'التشيخ'\n)\nORDER BY e.headword_norm, d.source_type;\n\" > /tmp/query1.json\ncat /tmp/query1.json | jq length\n"}}
